# good_slopes_fiber35_width3_rect4

Topic: elementary_number_theory   Node: 73ed421c9fae

Provenance: helper lemma. One normalized six-missing rectangle in the 35-point fiber route to OP-1027, tested in experiment 22048. The trimmed LRAT proof and its interpretation are checked by Lean.

No set of points over the residues modulo 35 can contain (0,0) and (1,34), have at most three points over each first coordinate, and make each of the directions 2, 3, 6, 8, 12, 13, 17, 18, 19, 22, 23, 24, 26, 27, 31, 32, 33 and 34 both injective and surjective on the set.
-/

